From 774f7aed6b7472d35f0028000420030d9fd686c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jjude80 <18168364+jjude80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:32:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(workspace): keep a refused child out of the holder's
 plugin workspace

The dispatch-time refusal stopped the local realization path from restoring
another issue's isolated workspace, and the pinned branch is dropped so the
child cannot find the holder's registered worktree by name.

The plugin preparation path still adopted the holder's workspace row.
prepareHeartbeatWorkspace passed issueRef.executionWorkspaceId to
preparePluginWorkspace, which restores that row and its saved provider
binding, so a refused child was handed the holder's storage through the
other door. The refusal now decides the workspace id that both preparation
paths use: a refused child gets no existing workspace id, and an issue that
owns its workspace keeps it.

The admission notice is emitted only for a refused reuse request, and it
states what was observed instead of promising a replacement. The duplicate
check asks the database for a bounded match instead of loading every
comment body of the issue into the process.

Tests: the policy suite covers the workspace id decision and the notice
rule, and the workspace session suite covers the id the plugin preparation
receives for a refused child and for an issue that owns its workspace.
